Assignment title: Visual prompt studio phase 1.2

Prompt: Create a poster for an acoustic music album cover where the picture is based on a cozy roam where the back wall has a bookcase filled with books and a few flower plants. Place an acoustic guitar in front of the bookshelf as if it’s leaning on it and make it the subject of the cover. Place a chair beside it with a denim jacket hanging off it. Show natural sunlight coming inside from the window on the left. Show how the light hits off the left side of the guitar, on the chair and through out the room and show the shapes of the shadow having different proportions and lengths according to where the light hits the object. Make it from the prospective from the farther right corner of the room, showing the window and the left side of the bookcase which aligns with the left wall seem smaller and the element are bigger the closer it gets from the point of prospective. Show a green grass field with dandelions through the open window but make it seem a bit farther in the distance. Use various lines and repetition of elements to make the cover feel more alive and make sure to include movement in the cover. For the movement, use the curtain on the window and show as if it is flowing because of the way the wind hit it making it flutter in the room. Use warm tones to show how the sunlight brings warmth in the room. The poster should have asymmetrical balance. Place the name of the album “Summer Times” in white cursive letters on the bottom of the cover.

Vocabulary breakdown:
Value – lightness and darkness of a tone of color that is used to indicate the mood and depth of any work.
Space – area surrounding an object in a composition that helps to give an idea of depth, distance, proportion between size of different objects, etc.
Unity – it refers to how all the elements of a work or composition come together to create one whole experience for the viewer.
Balance – it refers to how all the elements of a work or composition are spread out and distributed to different parts carrying different weight in the art.
Rhythm – it refers to a pattern or  that is followed and repeated in the composition in order to make it seem organized and not too crowded.


